  node [
    id 96
    label "TIDLH2ZOf54"
    step 0
    date "2021-04-14T14:16:25Z"
    title "How Blockchain Works  and What It Is | School of Block"
    description "You have one block. And then another one. And another. They&#8217;re linked forever in an unbreakable chain. Each one has been embedded with data that cannot be rewritten after the fact. But see how easily I can just remove this one block and break that chain? What can we use it for? Why hasn&#8217;t it been possible before and what exactly do we mean by consensus? Let&#8217;s find out.&#10;&#10;Sections in this video&#10;0:00&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203; Intro &#8211; hello, blockchain&#10;1:30&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203; A recap of crypto and an intro to blockchain&#10;5:04&#8203; Decision-making on the blockchain: consensus mechanisms&#10;5:33 The history of blockchain &#10;7:11 Byzantine General's Problem &#10;8:58 Public and private blockchains&#10;10:03&#8203;&#8203;&#8203; The future of blockchain&#10;11:25 There you have it!&#10;&#10;CHECK OUT SCHOOL OF BLOCK&#10;Ledger Academy: https://bit.ly/3jhLxiF&#10;&#10;FOLLOW LEDGER&#10;YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/ledger&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/ledger&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/Ledger&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/Ledger/"
