    description "#cryptology, #cryptography, #cryptanalysis, #blockchain&#10;&#10;In this video, we explain how blockchains, e.g. bitcoin, work. We describe in detail blocks, how these are mined in a blockchain, and how transactions are generated and executed in a crypto coin. Using our demo blockchain implemented in CrypTool 2, we simulate our very own blockchain and play with addresses, transactions, and mining.&#10;&#10;The blockchain simulation which we show in the video is now available in the current nightly build of CrypTool 2. It will also be available in the upcoming &#34;Christmas 2021 stable release&#34; of CrypTool 2.&#10;&#10;Here, you can find the json visualizer that I used in the video: http://jsonviewer.stack.hu/&#10;&#10;If you are interested in learning the fundaments of cryptology, let me invite you to have a look at our video series about the basics of cryptology, also for beginners: https://youtu.be/jbumW7Ym03o&#10;&#10;You can download the latest version of CrypTool 2 from here: https://www.cryptool.org/en/ct2/downloads"
    channeltitle "Cryptography for Everybody"
